# Soil Moisture Monitoring System

An ESP32-based soil moisture monitoring system designed to measure the moisture level of soil using a soil moisture sensor.

## Description

This project uses an ESP32 and a soil moisture sensor to monitor the moisture content of soil. The sensor provides a signal corresponding to the moisture level, which is read and processed by the ESP32.

The system can be used to monitor soil conditions and determine whether the soil requires watering.

## Components

- ESP32
- Soil Moisture Sensor
- Breadboard
- Jumper Wires
- USB Cable

## Working

1. The soil moisture sensor is placed in the soil.
2. The sensor detects the moisture level of the soil.
3. The sensor output is connected to an input pin of the ESP32.
4. The ESP32 reads the sensor value.
5. The moisture reading is used to determine the soil condition.

## Technologies Used

- ESP32
- Arduino IDE
- Embedded C/C++
- Soil Moisture Sensor

